ve `(size/11)*8` bytes: o `C3 86` (134 bytes) que o jogo manda ⇒ **96 bytes num buffer de 64** 💥 → `PacketSniffer.cpp`: agora só decodifica C3 com **SM ≤ 22 bytes** (buffer de 32). **b) DC** — o auto-potion injetava `C1 0x26` **puro**; suas capturas mostram que o jogo manda isso **dentro de um C3+SM** (numBytes=5). O servidor não entende um C1 0x26 no C→S → drop. → `PacketInjector`: uso de item agora passa pelo **mesmo pipeline C3+SM** da skill (`SendC3Sm`), e o `SM source = [serial] + innerC1[2..size]` bate exatamente com a captura. ## 2. \"Dizer o ID do item\" — implementado O servidor manda o inventário no login (`CItemManager::GCItemListSend` → **`F3 10`**), com `slot + ItemInfo(12)` por item. O byp agora parseia esse pacote e monta a tabela **slot → ID do item**: ``` POTION: lista de itens (F3 10): 7 item(ns) POTION: slot=22 item=0x0E01 POTION: slot=49 item=0x0E04 ``` Novo comando (o ID é **hex**): ``` POTION_CONFIG|hp=50|mp=30|interval=1000|hpitem=0E01|mpitem=0E04 ``` → no momento de usar, o byp resolve o slot pela tabela (`FindSlotByItemId`). O `POTION_STATUS` mostra `item de HP 0x0E01 -> slot 22` e `inventário conhecido: N item(ns)`. No MuProxy2, `PotionConfigMessage`/`PotionSer…\n- **Tools:** read_file, search_files, edit_file, run_command","vector":[0.011274502,0.056039155,-0.12814331,-0.016897103,0.06426101,-0.06457597,0.0654089,0.035629004,-0.06524345,-0.048855253,-0.05850305,0.019391844,0.09631516,-0.022078464,0.026070224,0.008476214,-0.02588155,-0.04253243,-0.0435482,0.05335677,0.01523721,-0.029358136,-0.04174125,0.036187146,0.095953226,0.02250555,0.010873417,0.04293875,-0.011122595,0.018125862,0.05309023,-0.0033211266,0.0030352506,-0.012839893,-0.0035647461,-0.057858225,0.043014057,-0.025779797,-0.0035124589,0.009070101,0.0039400323,-0.04420681,0.029526375,0.0060395175,0.044554554,0.05614869,0.03689678,0.030345252,0.07766874,-0.06602446,0.054106787,0.012177456,0.014455833,-0.0608996,0.074103825,0.079018496,-0.048964493,0.010649879,0.038691167,-0.01768