8,0.008559125,0.060271725,0.012052308,0.118012585,0.032455415,-0.028911907,0.0033427982,0.04040256,-0.03001207,0.0015572372,0.019828515,0.002221874,-0.054368947,0.016241588,-0.005140168,-0.032156825,-0.002151677,-0.0100944415,0.010138608,-0.0029511766,-0.033334527,0.0008026946,0.007401221,-0.0011930425,-0.016081495,0.009157165,0.017922472,-0.017441051,0.039530806,0.024444582,0.04420402,-0.015443567,0.018788908,-0.045833252,0.0038404395,0.0018584513,-0.025618128,-0.041114837,0.03716362,-0.039172743,0.04028985,-0.015048013,0.00957917,0.015763192,-0.03007793,0.018142628,0.0070453724,0.013858065,-0.017133405,-0.052941993,0.014656223,0.00053333724,-0.00029602254,-0.00840629,-0.013987983,-0.014410184,-0.027903797,-0.0027980676,-0.040072024,-0.053241134,0.049020253,0.022518607,-0.000034419718,-0.036496326,-0.0068490133,-0.03202145,-0.022476682,-0.018241266,0.04068568,-0.03626643,0.035779916,0.007985747,-0.001977958,-0.02621924,-0.00089680846,0.011937273,-0.018533628,0.055142332,-0.0097350795,-0.014600407,0.050611198,0.024957469,-0.010603332,-0.011847748,0.020691413,0.10745983,0.005939198,-0.023878114,-0.077801034,0.044828866,0.01541376,-0.0063466006,-0.0632372,-0.0023830424,0.009719873],"hash":"cf74cec:2105","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T03:25:32.381Z\n- **User:** [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [PACKETHANDLER] RECV linha (14): [POTION_START| ] [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [POTION] auto-potion LIGADO (hp<50% mp<30% intervalo=1000ms) [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [CRASH] === EXCEPTION FirstChance === [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [CRASH] Code: 0xC0000005 Flags: 0x00000000 Addr: 0x745F81C9 [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [CRASH] Module: F:\\blackrockmu\\byp.dll [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [CRASH] ModuleBase: 0x745F0000 EIP_RVA: 0x000081C9 [2026-11-15 19:22:01] [CRASH] EAX=0x3E8DF6B1 EBX=0x0C29DF70 ECX=0x562…\n- **Outcome:** **Achei a causa raiz de verdade** — e ela é do compilador, não do meu código. ## O que o `dumpbin` provou (código gerado) ``` 100081C2: mov dword ptr [ebp-4],0 ; estado do SEH = FORA do try 100081C9: mov eax,dword ptr [eax+14h] ; <<< CRASH (a leitura ficou DESPROTEGIDA) ``` **⇒ O MSVC `/O2` move loads para fora da região do `__try`** (ele assume \"carregar memória não lança exceção\" — falso). Por isso o `__except` **nunca** via a exceção: o ACCESS_VIOLATION acontecia *fora* da proteção. Ligar `/EHsc` (que também eliminatei o aviso `C4530` que existia desde sempre) **não resolve** — o problema é o *load hoisting*, não o unwind. ## A correção (não depende mais do `__try`) Novo `src/include/SafeRead.h`: **checagem explícita de memória com `VirtualQuery`** antes de cada leitura. Verificado no binário gerado: ``` 100082E7: call dword ptr [1000F030h] ; ← VirtualQuery 100082ED: cmp eax,1Ch / jne … ; falhou → retorna 0 100082F2: cmp dword ptr [esp+14h],1000h ; State == MEM_COMMIT? 100082FC: test dword ptr [esp+18h],101h ; PAGE_GUARD|PAGE_NOACCESS? ``` ⇒ **agora o load só acontece se a página for legível** → impossível dar AV. Convertido para `SafeRead`: `UserObject()`, `Character()`, **todos** os stats (`Life/MaxLife/Mana/…`), a **PartyList** (`PartyLife/PartyMaxLife/PartyLifePercent`) e o scan do array de objetos do viewport. `build.bat` ficou com `/EHsc` + `/MAP` (útil para mapear offsets de crash). ## O que espero no próximo teste 1. **`POTION_START` não deve crashar mais** — o AV …\n- **Tools:** write_file, edit_file, read_file, repl, run_command","vector":[0.0236557,0.037026003,-0.1600228,-0.04431146,0.074888274,-0.07046716,0.041411288,0.004597786,-0.010018739,-0.027006943,-0.039085113,0.045361422,0.06842736,-0.025876075,0.052207716,0.033964824,-0.026800415,-0.039639056,-0.07521808,-0.00037230612,0.019577663,-0.038118564,-0.034762636,-0.021815578,0.067977086,0.025686301,-0.013626139,0.040584758,-0.03878004,0.018145667,0.05789036,-0.029367406,-0.010247602,-0.017287802,-0.0043183356,-0.05286092,0.008829468,-0.03330036,-0.012295493,0.031808954,0.006654818,-0.007