565704,0.04222675,0.071316846,-0.0023895486,0.005947023,0.029470315,0.010712425,0.10268396,-0.020481028,-0.022650741,-0.0056378352,-0.01584716,-0.02124552,0.024395352,0.03247827,-0.028295415,-0.029547537,0.000039769664,-0.048085943,-0.02743516,-0.03360685,-0.03121133,-0.045718987,-0.01856246,-0.042001016,-0.0011026538,0.02400473,-0.0012101582,-0.033689935,-0.010572318,0.03712026,0.002321963,0.025713619,-0.00881949,0.025035715,-0.0036670906,0.052408088,-0.012930461,-0.0152187245,-0.008243438,-0.017620804,-0.04053079,-0.02259642,-0.03685071,-0.024972051,0.0010380237,0.04862989,-0.008646292,-0.06041384,-0.0090767825,0.010020118,0.017337307,-0.0070115486,-0.048224475,0.0102170715,0.023780461,-0.0032631967,0.03228708,-0.04999909,0.024947025,-0.011267013,-0.0067703417,-0.06291239,-0.034201205,0.050048437,0.013722041,-0.005167826,-0.011557848,0.0015732173,-0.031919178,-0.03923205,-0.05983249,0.034107115,-0.01663325,0.0331833,0.00006497979,-0.005751564,-0.057489157,0.0019911297,0.0064198417,-0.0051835016,0.049154136,-0.022265151,-0.055742946,0.019798065,0.015780827,0.01591021,0.0140732955,0.02650192,0.15272449,0.009888254,0.0061219586,-0.027314417,0.027286075,0.011503704,-0.013245237,-0.034553926,-0.020040914,-0.00277589],"hash":"16df04a6:2189","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":false},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T14:25:06.315Z\n- **User:** /openspec:apply\n- **Outcome:** Apliquei a mudança. **A causa raiz era uma coisa mínima**: o `C4`. ## O que eu descobri Reimplementei o SimpleModulus em Python e testei offline com a chave de recepção do log — o **C3 do login decodifica perfeitamente**: ``` RECV #15 C3 len=233 chave=recv plaintext=00 F3 03 25 34 07 ... ← o F3 03 (character info) RECV #16 C4 len=784 ← O INVENTÁRIO ESTÁ AQUI ``` E no log do byp (build anterior) já aparecia `C3-SM decodificado len=167 : 00 F3 03 25 34 07 ...` — **a decifra S→C funcionava**. O que faltava era: > **`F3 10` (lista de itens) vem num C4 de 784 bytes** (≈60 itens × 13 bytes), e o `C4` tem header de **3 bytes** (C4, sizeHi, sizeLo) — o `TryDecodeSmBody` só tratava `C3` (2 bytes). Por isso o inventário nunca chegava, e sem ele o byp não tinha como saber qual slot tem potion. ## O que implementei (Fases 1–4) | Fase | Entrega | |---|---| | 1 | `TryDecodeSmBody` trata **C4** (header 3 bytes); buffer de decifra 512 → **2048** (o C4 de 784 decifra 568) | | 2 | `F3 10` → `slot → item ID` (o `DecodeItemId` do byp já batia com o `ItemByteConvert` do servidor — conferi) | | 3 | **Slots de HP/MP descobertos pelo ID** (`7168..7171` = HP, `7172..7174` = MP, elite `7238/7239`) → escolha automática, **sem beber potion nunca** | | 4 | **`VerifyAutoUse()`**: se o uso não produziu efeito em 900ms → o slot está vazio → **troca para o próximo do mesmo tipo** (round-robin) e registra no log; sem mais slots → avisa e **para de injetar** (hoje ele martela o slot morto e o log mente) | O le…\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file, edit_file, manage_todos","vector":[0.017585125,0.030263087,-0.14217892,-0.07105349,0.055446383,-0.05889011,0.050470013,0.018089205,-0.051219285,-0.059417456,-0.06669727,0.014624272,0.061062947,-0.018684078,0.024027651,0.0058840583,-0.016775344,-0.064502284,-0.02754593,0.06069472,0.029344125,-0.047376245,-0.040272918,-0.004262184,0.08070829,0.028621003,0.015151483,0.041199397,-0.04482682,-0.017974582,0.01719035,0.0025422287,0.015722284,-0.032963675,0.0037186483,-0.05728527,0.058365833,-0.009136146,0.018000854,0.02956475,-0.009361756,-0.01575745,0.021463508,0.0287705,0.044764183,0.013117575,0.048881173,0.0015537251,0.047306087,-0.11047344,0.04109816,0.011926574,0.01528136,-0.039509088,0.07296462,0.037128985,-0.03329097,0.019861557,0.04672336,-0.017653,0.108680844,0.013133164,-0.013247898,0.070543475,0.022448119,-0.0112792775,-0.024237694,0.04216034,-0.025684293,-0.00401911,0.054330222,-0.016884953,0.0042282185,-0.01933932,-0.020812092,-0.018060466,-0.08069678,-0.050851565,-0.0033151514,-0.0